      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "add whatsapp outbound token diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOutbound WhatsApp direct sends can fail silently when WhatsApp Web needs trusted-contact token state or LID routing data for a recipient.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, Codex helped update this branch and evidence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds outbound token diagnostics and LID-aware lookup paths around WhatsApp Web sends.\n\nThe send path now:\n\n- resolves phone-number targets through Baileys LID lookup and USync when possible\n- persists discovered PN/LID mappings for later sends\n- checks trusted-contact token state before direct sends\n- reports reachout timelock and new-chat quota diagnostics when a token is missing\n- keeps socket operations bounded by the existing WhatsApp socket timing wrapper\n- lets token-backed direct sends pass the monitor reachout-timelock gate\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get clearer failures instead of accepted-but-undelivered direct WhatsApp sends, and already-known LID mappings are reused for later outbound messages.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `0f9a802dbfacb5fc502a1964d9ac6f21e119ac4c`\nCurrent base checked locally: `b0ebb81e89f5217397d409c996e2bbf914623a94` (`origin/main`)\n\nThis update merged current `origin/main` into the PR branch. The merge applied cleanly.\n\nLatest validation:\n\n- `mkdir -p .tmp && TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.tmp\" node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-whatsapp.config.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/socket-timing.test.ts` - 2 files, 56 tests passed\n- `git diff --cached --check` - passed before commit\n- `git diff --check` - passed before commit\n\nEarlier validation in this sweep:\n\n- `codex review --base origin/main` on the prior latest-base push found no concrete actionable regression; bundled autoreview could not run because the diff contains secret-like content.\n- `node scripts/test-extension.mjs whatsapp` failed locally with filesystem write/quota errors (`Unknown system error -122, write`) in media/session/call tests. Re-running the touched send-api/socket tests with repo-local `TMPDIR` passed.\n- Local Testbox/Crabbox was unavailable in this sweep, so these were local wrapper checks.\n",
